Provide a fallback scan when an index is unavailable or invalid, subject to configured resource limits.

Do not claim that every query reads only one chunk. Explain when an index or predicate allows that optimization and when a scan is required.

Avoid maintaining duplicate data structures that create correctness risks without a measurable performance benefit.

