# 20. Caching

Add caching only where it preserves documented consistency behavior.

Reasonable candidates include:

- Repository metadata
- Table schemas
- Registry manifests
- Immutable chunk contents
- Read-only indexes

Immutable chunks may be cached by content hash. Mutable manifests need stronger invalidation rules.

Do not treat a warm serverless instance as persistent shared storage. Serverless memory is an optimization, never the system of record.

Document cache lifetime, invalidation behavior, and what happens after a write from another process.

