# 24. Definition of Done

The first release is complete only when the following criteria have been met or transparently marked as incomplete:

- [ ] Native JavaScript core with no mandatory third-party runtime dependencies.
- [ ] Relational and document engines have separate, tested implementations.
- [ ] Local storage provider works without external credentials.
- [ ] GitHub provider implements the documented operations.
- [ ] Data files use a documented, versioned format.
- [ ] Chunking never splits records arbitrarily.
- [ ] Metadata includes integrity and version information.
- [ ] Point lookups can use primary-key indexes.
- [ ] Supported query operators produce correct results.
- [ ] CRUD tests pass for both engines.
- [ ] Concurrency conflicts are detected or safely prevented within the declared model.
- [ ] Large imports respect serverless body and execution limits.
- [ ] Import retries do not silently duplicate records.
- [ ] Exports generate valid JSON, JSON Lines, and CSV.
- [ ] Dashboard credentials remain server-side.
- [ ] API routes enforce authentication and authorization.
- [ ] Error handling does not disclose secrets.
- [ ] The CLI runs using the same engine.
- [ ] Documentation explains consistency, cost, and storage limits.
- [ ] All implemented tests have been run and their results reported.
- [ ] The product does not claim features or guarantees that have not been verified.

